          "date": "2026-11-20 03:48:37.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-18133 tests: check setstripe in sanity 398m",
        "message": "LU-18133 tests: check setstripe in sanity 398m\n\nsanity 398m ignores the result of \"lfs setstripe -o 0,1,0,1\".\nWhen it fails (ENOSPC is seen in CI, as the MDS can still see an OST\nas full after a preceding test), the file gets default striping, the\ninjected bulk write failure never hits the first stripe and the test\nreports that the dio write succeeded.\n\nFix the cleanup traps in 398l (and add them to 398k) so deletes\ncomplete before the MDS/OST sync wait, leaving later tests a correct\nview of OST space. In 398m, wait for deletes and MDS/OST sync, retry\nsetstripe for up to 30 seconds, and fail with a clear error if it\nnever works.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"398l 398m\"\nFixes: 9435453d7965 (\"LU-17919 tests: wait to resolve ENOSPC in sanity 398l\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: If1969dd8097a9edf9137bfe95a80064dea1c87ce\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70633\nReviewed-by: Chakshu Kansal <ckansal@ddn.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
